 "もの": "أُقْنُوم (An individual who has been granted personhood; usually a human being.) / فَرْد (The physical body of a being seen as distinct from the mind, character, etc.)  [person]\nrarely used without a qualifier\nمثال: じっくり彼に耳を貸す者はいない。\n→ No one stops to listen to him.",
 "ものあんじ": "قَلَق (An unpleasant state of mental uneasiness, nervousness, apprehension and obsessio) / قَلَق, اِضْطِرَاب الْقَلَق (A state of restlessness and agitation, often accompanied by a distressing sense )  [anxiety]",
 "ものいい": "[manner of speaking] / [verbal argument] / اِعْتَرَاض (The act of objecting.) / اِعْتَرَاض (A statement expressing opposition, or a reason or cause for expressing oppositio) / اِعْتِرَاض (An official protest raised in a court of law during a legal trial over a violati)  [objection] / إِشَاعَة, شَائِعَة (A statement or claim of questionable accuracy, from no known reliable source, us)  [rumor]",
 "ものいう": "تَكَلَّمَ, تَحَدَّثَ (To communicate, usually by means of speech.) / مُحَاضَرَة (A lecture.) / خِطَاب (A major topic of social discussion.) / مُحَادَثَات, مُفَاوَضَات (Meeting to discuss a particular matter.)  [to talk]\nمثال: 物言えば唇寒し・馬鹿ほど言いたがる。\n→ He knows most who speaks least.",
 "ものいえばくちびるさむしあきのかぜ": "اَلسُّكُوتُ مِن ذَهَبٍ (Peace and quiet have great value.)  [silence is golden]",
 "ものいり": "صَرْف, مَصْرُوف (A spending or consuming, often a disbursement of funds.)  [expenses] / غَالٍ, الْغَالِي (Having a high price or cost.)  [expensive]",
 "ものいれ": "حَاوِيَة (Someone who contains; something that contains.)  [container]\nمثال: 彼女はタオルをきれいにたたみ、それを物入れに仕舞った。\n→ She folded up the towels and put them away in the cupboard.",
 "ものうい": "سَوْدَاوِيَّة (Great sadness or depression, especially of a thoughtful or introspective nature.)  [melancholy]\nمثال: そして、どうすることも出来ない物憂さに、ふっとため息をつく。\n→ And then I breathe a sigh from melancholy in being unable to do anything about it.",
 "ものうげ": "[languorous ; weary] / كَئِيب, مُوحِش (Suffering from gloom; melancholy; dejected.)  [gloomy]",
 "ものうり": "جَوَّال, بَائِع مُتَجَوِّل (An itinerant seller of small goods.)  [peddler]",
 "ものおしみ": "بُخْل (The property of being stingy: a lack of generosity; excessive parsimony.)  [stinginess]",
 "ものおじ": "تَوَتُّر (The state or quality of being nervous.)  [nervousness]\noft. in negative form",
 "ものおそろしい": "مُخيف, مُخيفة (Eerie, or suggestive of ghosts or the supernatural.)  [spooky]",
 "ものおと": "ضَوْضَاء, ضَجِيج (Various sounds, usually unwanted or unpleasant.)  [noise]\nمثال: 少年は物音に震えた。\n→ The boy quivered at the sound.",
 "ものおぼえ": "ذَاكِرَة, حَافِظَة (The ability of the brain to record information or impressions with the facility ) / ذِكْرَى (A record of a thing or an event stored and available for later use by an organis) / ذَاكِرَة (The part of a computer that stores variable executable code or data (RAM) or una)  [memory]\nمثال: この子は物覚えが早い。\n→ The child is learning quickly.",
 "ものおもい": "قَلَق (An unpleasant state of mental uneasiness, nervousness, apprehension and obsessio) / قَلَق, اِضْطِرَاب الْقَلَق (A state of restlessness and agitation, often accompanied by a distressing sense )  [anxiety]\nمثال: 私の父は物思いにふけっていた。\n→ My father was lost in thought.",
