 "より": "مِن (Introduces a comparison, and is associated with comparatives, and with words suc)  [than]\nمثال: 柔道では力より技のほうが大切である。\n→ In judo, technique is more important than strength. / بَدَلًا مِن (Used to indicate that the following alternative is less preferred.) / أَكْثَر مِن, عَنّ (Instead of; in preference to.)  [rather than]\nمثال: 私は金よりむしろ名誉を選ぶ。\n→ I would choose honor before money. / مِن (Used to indicate source or provenance.) / مِن, عَنْ (Indicating differentiation.)  [from]\nمثال: ７月１０日より札幌支店を開設いたします。\n→ On July 10, we will open our Sapporo branch. / اِسْتَثْنَى (To exclude; to specify as being an exception.) / إِلَّا, بِاسْتِثْنَاء (Used to introduce an exception or qualification to something previously stated.) / إِلَّا (Used to introduce a clause, phrase, verb infinitive, adverb or other non-noun co)  [except]\nwith neg. sentence; as よりほかに...ない, よりしかたがない, etc.\nمثال: もうこれよりほかに手はない。\n→ There's no other way than this now.",
 "よりあい": "اِجْتِمَاع, مَجْلِس (A gathering of persons for a purpose; an assembly.) / مُلَاقَاة, مُقَابَلَة (An encounter between people, even accidental.) / مُلَاقَاة, لِقَاء (An administrative unit in the Religious Society of Friends (Quakers).)  [meeting] / [village assembly] / [two wrestlers approaching each other]",
 "よりあう": "جَمَعَ (To bring parts of a whole closer.)  [to gather]",
 "よりあわせる": "اِنْضَفَرَ, تَدَاخَلَ (To become twined together.)  [to intertwine]",
 "よりいい": "أَفْضَل, أَحْسَن (comparative degree of good and well) / حَسَّنَ (To improve.) / تَحَسَّنَ (To become better; to improve.)  [better]\nمثال: 彼はより良い生活を求めてブラジルに移住した。\n→ He immigrated to Brazil in search of a better life.",
 "よりいっそう": "[still more ; even more]\nمثال: 彼女には欠点があるから僕はより一層彼女が好きだ。\n→ I love her all the more for her faults. / زَاد (To make (a quantity, etc.) larger.) / زِيَادَة (An amount by which a quantity is increased.) / اِرْتِفَاع, اِزْدِيَاد (For a quantity, the act or process of becoming larger.)  [increased]",
