 "よりか": "مِن (Introduces a comparison, and is associated with comparatives, and with words suc)  [than] / بَدَلًا مِن (Used to indicate that the following alternative is less preferred.) / أَكْثَر مِن, عَنّ (Instead of; in preference to.)  [rather than]\nمثال: 仕事をしているというよりかは、ただ会社にいるだけって感じ。\n→ Instead of being here to work, you get the sense that he's simply a permanent fixture here. / مِن (Used to indicate source or provenance.) / مِن, عَنْ (Indicating differentiation.)  [from] / اِسْتَثْنَى (To exclude; to specify as being an exception.) / إِلَّا, بِاسْتِثْنَاء (Used to introduce an exception or qualification to something previously stated.) / إِلَّا (Used to introduce a clause, phrase, verb infinitive, adverb or other non-noun co)  [except]\nwith neg. sentence; as よりかほかに...ない, よりかしかたがない, etc.",
 "よりくず": "زُبَالَة, نُفَايَات (Useless physical things to be discarded; rubbish; refuse.) / سَلُّة الْمُهْمَلَات (A container into which things are discarded.)  [trash]",
