 "よりも": "مِن (Introduces a comparison, and is associated with comparatives, and with words suc)  [than]\nemphatic form of より\nمثال: 健康はお金よりも大切だよ。\n→ Health is more important than money. / بَدَلًا مِن (Used to indicate that the following alternative is less preferred.) / أَكْثَر مِن, عَنّ (Instead of; in preference to.)  [rather than]\nمثال: 人の幸福は財産よりも人間性で決まる。\n→ A man's happiness depends on what he is rather than on what he has.",
