 "よろける": "تَرَنُّح (An unsteady movement of the body in walking or standing as if one were about to ) / تَرَنَّحَ (To sway unsteadily, reel, or totter.)  [to stagger]\nمثال: その老人は足がもつれてよろけた。\n→ The old man tripped over his own feet.",
 "よろこばしい": "سَعِيد, مُفْرِح (Feeling or causing joy.)  [joyful (news, event, etc.)]\nمثال: この喜ばしい日をお祝いし、幸せと喜びがあなたにきますように。\n→ May happiness and joy come to you as you celebrate this joyous day.",
 "よろこばす": "فُرْجَة (Joy; pleasure.)  [to delight]\nمثال: その少年は両親を喜ばした。\n→ The boy made his parents happy.",
 "よろこび": "سُرُور, فَرَح (A feeling of extreme happiness or cheerfulness, especially related to the acquis)  [joy]\nمثال: 我々はお互いに喜びをわかちあった。\n→ We partook in each other's joy.",
 "よろこびごと": "اِحْتِفَال (The formal performance of a solemn rite, such as Christian sacrament.) / اِحْتِفَال, مِهْرَجَان (A social gathering for entertainment and fun; a party.)  [celebration]",
 "よろこぶ": "أَفْرَحَ (To make happy, exhilarate.)  [to rejoice]\nمثال: 彼は母親の到着を喜んだ。\n→ He rejoiced at his mother's arrival. / هَنَّأَ, يُهَنِّئُ (To express one’s sympathetic pleasure or joy to the person(s) it is felt for)  [to congratulate] / أَهْلًا وَسَهْلًا, مَرْحَبًا (Greeting given upon someone's arrival.) / تَرْحِيب (The act of greeting someone’s arrival, especially by saying \"Welcome!\"; receptio) / رَحَّبَ, اِسْتَقْبِل (To affirm or greet the arrival of someone, especially by saying \"Welcome!\".)  [to welcome (a proposal, advice, etc.)] / [to do with pleasure ; to do gladly]\nas よろこんで...\nمثال: 喜んで質問に答えましょう。\n→ I'll be happy to answer your question.",
