 "よろしい": "حَسَن, جَيِّد (Of a person or an animal:) / حَسَن, جَيِّد (Of a capability:) / صِحِّيّ (Of a property or quality:) / حَسَنًا (That is good; an elliptical exclamation of satisfaction or commendation.) / خَيْر (The forces or behaviours that are the enemy of evil. Usually consists of helping) / سِلْعَة (An item of merchandise.)  [good]\nمثال: あなたに頼んでもよろしいですか。\n→ May I request a favour of you?",
 "よろしおす": "حَسَّن, لَطِيف (Pleasant, satisfactory, complimentary.)  [nice]",
 "よろしく": "حَسَنًا, بِخَيْر (Accurately, competently, satisfactorily.) / حَسَنًا, بِخَيْر (Completely, fully.) / حَسَنًا, بِخَيْر (To a significant degree.) / بِخَيْر (In good health.) / طيّب (used to introduce a statement that may be contrary to expect) / حسنًا (used to introduce a statement that may be contrary to expect) / بِئْر, بير (A hole sunk into the ground as a source of water, oil, natural gas or other flui) / عَيْن, بِئْر (A place where a liquid such as water surfaces naturally; a spring.)  [well] / مَعَ أَطْيَب التَحْيَات (Used as a polite closing of a letter)  [best regards]\nمثال: ご家族の皆さんによろしく。\n→ Give my love to your family. / [just like ... ; as though one were ...]\nas ...よろしく / طَبْعًا (Naturally; as would be expected; for obvious reasons, obviously.)  [of course]\nas よろしく…べし",
