 "わきづくえ": "رَجَعَ, عَادَ (To come or go back (to a place or person).) / أَرْجَعَ, أَعَادَ (To give something back to its original holder or owner.) / عَوْدَة (The act of returning.)  [return]",
 "わきでる": "تَدَفُّق (the movement of a fluid) / تَدَفَّقَ, سَالَ (To move as a fluid from one position to another.)  [to flow (out)]\nمثال: 地面から水が沸き出ている。\n→ The water is welling up from the ground. / [to well up (of tears, emotions, etc.) ; to flow out (of tears)]\nمثال: その女の子の目から涙がわきでた。\n→ Tears welled up in the girl's eyes. / ظَهَرَ (To come into view.)  [to emerge]\nمثال: 人間の胸に希望は永遠にわき出る。\n→ Hope springs eternal in the human breast.",
