 "わきまえ": "[discernment ; discretion] / عِلْم, مَعْرِفَة (The fact of knowing about something; general understanding or familiarity with a) / عِلْم, مَعْرِفَة (Awareness of a particular fact or situation; a state of having been informed or )  [knowledge]",
 "わきまえる": "مَيَّزَ (To set apart as being different; to mark as different; to separate from another )  [to discriminate]\nمثال: 私たちが意識してほかの礼儀正しさの形をわきまえることが大切である。\n→ Therefore it is important for us to be aware of other forms of politeness. / عَلِمَ, عَرَفَ (To perceive the truth or factuality of; to be certain of; to be certain that.) / دَرَى, عَرَفَ (To have knowledge; to have information, be informed.)  [to know (manners, one's place, etc.)]\nمثال: 身分をわきまえなさい。\n→ Remember your station in life.",
