 "わらいごえ": "ضَحِك, ضِحْك (The sound of laughing, produced by air so expelled; any similar sound.)  [(sound of) laughter]\nمثال: 彼女の笑い声が家にこだました。\n→ Her laughter echoed through the house.",
 "わらう": "ضَحْكَة (An expression of mirth particular to the human species; the sound heard in laugh) / ضَحِكَ, ضحك (To show mirth, satisfaction, or derision, by peculiar movement of the muscles of)  [to laugh]\nمثال: クラスのもの皆が彼の冗談に笑った。\n→ The whole class laughed at his joke. / اِبْتِسَامَة, بَسْمَة (A facial expression comprised by flexing the muscles of both ends of one's mouth) / اِبْتَسَمَ (To have (a smile) on one's face.)  [to smile]\nمثال: しかし、彼はめったに笑いませんでした。\n→ But he did not often smile. / تَهَكَّمَ, سَخِرَ (To criticize or disapprove of someone or something through scornful jocularity; )  [to ridicule]\nesp. 嗤う\nمثال: ベェーだっ！乙女のことを嗤った罰よ！\n→ Pfft! That's what you get for laughing at a girl! / [to be dumbfounded ; to be flabbergasted]\nas 笑ってしまう or 笑っちゃう",
