 "ゟ": "مِن (Introduces a comparison, and is associated with comparatives, and with words suc)  [than]\nمثال: 柔道では力より技のほうが大切である。\n→ In judo, technique is more important than strength. / بَدَلًا مِن (Used to indicate that the following alternative is less preferred.) / أَكْثَر مِن, عَنّ (Instead of; in preference to.)  [rather than]\nمثال: 私は金よりむしろ名誉を選ぶ。\n→ I would choose honor before money. / مِن (Used to indicate source or provenance.) / مِن, عَنْ (Indicating differentiation.)  [from]\nمثال: ７月１０日より札幌支店を開設いたします。\n→ On July 10, we will open our Sapporo branch. / اِسْتَثْنَى (To exclude; to specify as being an exception.) / إِلَّا, بِاسْتِثْنَاء (Used to introduce an exception or qualification to something previously stated.) / إِلَّا (Used to introduce a clause, phrase, verb infinitive, adverb or other non-noun co)  [except]\nwith neg. sentence; as よりほかに...ない, よりしかたがない, etc.\nمثال: もうこれよりほかに手はない。\n→ There's no other way than this now.",
 "ア": "[sub- ; second-rate] / ـِيّ (suffix to form adjectives)  [-ous (indicating a low oxidation state)] / آسِيَا, أسيا (The largest continent, located east of Europe (typically delimited by the Urals))  [Asia] / الْأَرْجَنْتِين, الأرجنتين (A country in South America. Official name: Argentine Republic. Capital: Buenos A)  [Argentina]",
