 "アっ": "آه (An expression of relief, relaxation, comfort, confusion, understanding, wonder, )  [ah]\nexpression of surprise, recollection, etc.\nمثال: あっ、いけない！忘れるところだった！\n→ Oh, no! I almost forgot! / [hey!]\nused to get someone's attention",
 "アァ": "[ah! ; oh!]\nocc. written as 嗚呼, 噫 or 嗟\nمثال: ああ悲しい。\n→ Ah, me! / بَلَى, مبلا (Used to indicate disagreement or dissent in reply to a negative statement.) / نَعَم, نَعَمَانِ (An affirmative expression; an answer that shows agreement or acceptance.)  [yes]\nمثال: 彼女に疲れているのかと聞かれて彼は「ああ」といった。\n→ He said \"Yeah\" when she asked if he was tired. / [aah ; gah]\nin exasperation\nمثال: ああ、また失敗した。\n→ Ah, I've failed again! / [hey! ; yo!]\nمثال: ああ飛行機が離陸する。\n→ Look! There's a plane taking off.",
 "アア": "[ah! ; oh!]\nocc. written as 嗚呼, 噫 or 嗟\nمثال: ああ悲しい。\n→ Ah, me! / بَلَى, مبلا (Used to indicate disagreement or dissent in reply to a negative statement.) / نَعَم, نَعَمَانِ (An affirmative expression; an answer that shows agreement or acceptance.)  [yes]\nمثال: 彼女に疲れているのかと聞かれて彼は「ああ」といった。\n→ He said \"Yeah\" when she asked if he was tired. / [aah ; gah]\nin exasperation\nمثال: ああ、また失敗した。\n→ Ah, I've failed again! / [hey! ; yo!]\nمثال: ああ飛行機が離陸する。\n→ Look! There's a plane taking off.",
